  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen-blkback: Avoid UAF when reading I/O statistics\n\nReading I/O statistics via sysfs concurrently with tearing down a\nfrontend device might result in UAF or a NULL dereference, as the\nreading of the statistics data is not synchronized with freeing the\ndata.\n\nUse a rwlock for synchronizing.\n\nThis is XSA-528 / CVE-2026-100082",
